 ],
 "notes": "Disabled-by-default (no topic/policy/rule created) is expressed as gated declarations; absence of the planned resources cannot be asserted (exists.min>=1). Cloud Posse label conventions are recognised by the label input variables (namespace/stage/tenant/context) or by the Namespace/Stage tags the label module emits; generic 'name'/'environment' variables alone do not count. Region: the plan carries the provider region only with newer AWS providers, so a detector without a planned region attribute is accepted (Partial). Omitting datasources does not turn S3 protection off (new detectors enable it), so that encoding fails s3_protection_off by design. Every declared event rule, topic and topic policy must be gated (quantifier all); exists cannot take min 0 and an always-false 'all' check would pass the empty template, so planned absence is not asserted directly. GLM53F omits the S3 data source entirely, which leaves S3 protection on for a new detector; s3_protection_off is kept failing it."
}